---
title: Beef Goulash
servings: 4
course: Main
source: Recipes for the Kenwood Cooking Chef <urn:isbn:9780955847288>
prep time: 10m
cook time: 4h
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Hungarian
---

Slice the @onion{4%large} in the #food processor{} using the #thick slicing disc{} on speed 5.

Put the @oil{4%tbsp} in the bowl, attach the #stirring tool{}, set the temperature to 140°C, and the speed to stirring 1. When hot add the onions, @garlic{3%cloves}, and @white wine vinegar{2%tsp}. Cook for ~{5%minutes}.

Reduce the speed to stirring speed 2. Add the @braising steak{600%g}(cut into 2 cm cubes), @hot smoked paprika{1%tbsp}, @paprika{2%tbsp}, @ground coriander{0.5%tbsp}, @bay leaves{2%leaves}, @chopped tomatoes{1%tin × 400 g}, @tomato purée{200%g}, and @beef stock{120%ml}. Attach the #splashguard, set the temperature to 90°C, and cook for ~{3%hours}. If including @?sweet peppers{3} then add them half way through the cooking time.

If the meat needs longer then reset the temperature to 90°C and to stirring 2 for a further ~{1%hour}.

To thicken make a paste with the @?cornflour{1%tbsp} and a little water, add to the goulash. Add @salt and @pepper if necessary.

Serve with @sour cream{}, @rice, and @green salad{}.